## Architecture

```
Browser (single-page app: app.js, ECharts, Leaflet)
        │  JSON blocks over HTTPS, HttpOnly JWT cookie
        ▼
FastAPI server (server.py, uvicorn)  ──►  SQLite (users, tickets, quotes, chats, audit)
        │                                      ▲
        │ GPU models (loaded at startup)        │
        ├─ Qwen2.5 LLM  (Copilot explanations)  │
        ├─ NLLB-200     (translation)           │
        └─ Sentence embedder + reranker (RAG)   │
                                                │
Background worker (worker.py): simulator, agent cycles, escalation, feed threads
```

Pages are Python functions that return JSON "blocks"; the front end renders them and updates only what changed. The server and the heavy worker run in separate processes so the GPU models never share a GIL with the simulator.

## Tech stack

| Layer | Tools |
|---|---|
| Backend | Python, FastAPI, uvicorn, SQLite |
| AI / ML | Qwen2.5 (Instruct), NLLB-200 (distilled 600M), sentence-transformers, scikit-learn, Prophet (optional), LangGraph |
| Search | Own BM25 implementation + dense retrieval + cross-encoder rerank |
| Frontend | Vanilla JS single-page app, ECharts, Leaflet, TopoJSON (all bundled, no CDN at runtime) |
| Reports | reportlab, matplotlib, pdfplumber |
| Auth | PBKDF2, PyJWT, HttpOnly cookies |
| Runtime | Google Colab with a T4 GPU |

## Roles and page access

| Role | Copilot | Route | Quotes | Carriers | Weather | Margin | Customs | Run agents | Users |
|---|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|
| Admin | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| Operations Manager | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ |
| Freight Broker | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ |
| Auditor | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ |
| Customer | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ |

- Menu-level access is defined in one place and used by both the sidebar and the API guards.
- Action-level capabilities (`view`, `resolve`, `approve`, `run`, `feeder`, `admin`, `quote`) are enforced inside the Command Center.
- **Sign-up** offers Operations Manager, Freight Broker, Auditor and Customer only. Admin accounts are seeded, never self-registered, and the server rejects any other role.
- **Admins cannot lock, unlock or deactivate admin accounts**, including their own. Blocked attempts are written to the audit log.

## AI Copilot

The Copilot answers in layers, and each layer is plain Python you can read and extend:

1. **Small talk** — greetings, thanks, "what can you do".
2. **Typo repair** — fuzzy-corrects words against the vocabulary of the app's tables, columns, places and names.
3. **Conversation memory** — follow-ups such as "and CAR-010?" or "top 10 instead" use the previous turn.
4. **Smart intents** — daily briefing, compare two entities, entity profile, export, show SQL.
5. **Exact engine** — `analyst.py` explanations, then `qa.py` (whitelisted natural language to SQL).
6. **Presentation** — auto chart, follow-up suggestions, "interpreted as" note, CSV export, thumbs feedback.

Questions the Copilot cannot answer are logged. An Admin opens **Admin → Teach Copilot**, tests a list of questions, writes the correct answer with keywords, and the Copilot answers it (and rephrased versions) from then on. The starter set lives in `taught_seed.csv`. The Copilot also has a **Knowledge base** tab (RAG over policy documents) and a **Document translator** tab.

## Security

- PBKDF2 password hashing and progressive lockout (5 min, then 15 min, then permanent after repeated wrong passwords).
- Security-question password reset and optional e-mail OTP.
- HttpOnly JWT cookie sessions.
- Request IDs, JSON access log, security headers (CSP, frame, permissions) and per-IP rate limits on auth routes.
- A global error handler that never leaks tracebacks, plus Prometheus-style metrics.
- Retention, PII inventory, masking and data-subject export / erase (`privacy.py`).
- Read-only, parameterised SQL for the Copilot.

## Getting started (Google Colab)

**Requirements:** a Google account and a Colab runtime with a **T4 GPU** (Runtime → Change runtime type → T4 GPU).

1. Open `Milestone3.ipynb` in Google Colab and select the T4 GPU runtime.
2. *(Optional)* Add Colab Secrets (see below). `HF_TOKEN` speeds up model downloads.
3. Run all cells from top to bottom:
   - installs the dependencies,
   - writes the application files to `/content/app`,
   - bundles the front-end libraries and sign-in picture,
   - starts the server and the background worker.
4. Click the **Open the app** link printed by the launcher cell. If you saved `NGROK_AUTHTOKEN`, an ngrok fallback link is shown as well.
5. Sign in. In demo mode the admin account is:

   | Field | Value |
   |---|---|
   | E-mail | `admin@infosys.com` |
   | Password | `Admin@123` (or your `ADMIN_PASSWORD` secret) |

The first minutes show "Starting up" on the sign-in card while the models load on the GPU. You can already sign in during that time.

**Running outside Colab:** copy the generated `app/` folder, install the packages from the install cell and run `uvicorn server:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000`, then open `http://localhost:8000`.

## Configuration and secrets

Set these in Colab Secrets (or as environment variables):

| Name | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `HF_TOKEN` | Hugging Face token for faster model downloads |
| `JWT_SECRET_KEY` | Session signing key (a random one is generated and kept beside the database if not set) |
| `ADMIN_EMAIL_ID`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD` | Seeded admin account |
| `DEMO_MODE` | `1` (default) seeds demo accounts; `0` creates only the admin |
| `LLM_MODEL`, `NLLB_MODEL` | Override the default models |
| `NGROK_AUTHTOKEN` | Fallback public URL |
| `EMAIL_ID`, `EMAIL_PASSWORD`, `ALERT_EMAIL_TO` | E-mail OTP and alerts |
| `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL`, `TEAMS_WEBHOOK_URL`, `TWILIO_*` | Optional alert channels |

**Persistence:** with `PERSIST = True` in the launcher cell, the database (users, tickets, approvals and saved Copilot chats) is backed up to `MyDrive/freight_quote_data/db` every few minutes and restored automatically after a runtime reset.

**Ingest API:** `POST /ingest/<table>` with the `X-API-Key` printed by the launcher cell.

## Project structure

The notebook writes the application into `/content/app`:

```
app/
├── server.py            FastAPI routes, auth guards, page dispatch
├── worker.py            Background simulator, agent cycles, escalation
├── authx.py             Passwords, lockout, sessions, reset
├── hardening.py         Rate limits, headers, error handler, metrics
├── domain_freight.py    Freight agents, ML pricing, vessel tracking, rerouting
├── live_engine.py       Shared live agent runtime
├── live_rbac.py         Action-level capabilities
├── seanav.py            Sea routing (ocean mask, canals, Dijkstra)
├── sim_plus.py, sim_fq.py, mc.py, mc_sims.py   Simulators and Monte Carlo
├── twin.py, twin2.py    Digital Twin
├── copilot_pro.py       Copilot layers
├── qa.py, analyst.py    Exact SQL engine and explanations
├── rag.py, kb_pack.py   Hybrid RAG and sample policy pack
├── gpu.py               Qwen, NLLB and embedder loading
├── data_feeder.py       Upload / folder / URL feeds
├── reports.py           PDF and CSV reports
├── privacy.py           Retention, masking, export / erase
├── persist.py           Drive backup of the database
├── views_*.py, blocks.py   Server-driven pages and UI blocks
├── seed_data.py, scale_data.py, taught_seed.csv   Seed and starter data
└── static/              index.html, style.css, app.js, vendor libraries
```

